{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And all the people saw the voices.</b> This 'seeing' has the sense of apprehension, as in (Genesis 27:27) ״ראה ריח בני״ — 'See the smell of my son' — for voice and smell are not literally seen. Or one may say רואים because the voice came in fire, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 29:7): ״קול ה׳ חוצב להבות אש״ — 'The voice of YHWH hews flames of fire' — and they saw the fire, and therefore it says רואים את הקולות, 'they saw the voices.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:38.721992013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}